A||||8||V8Fiero||Need help with flushmounts.........TOM?||||5||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||03-24-2001||06:43 PM||||OK...Got a set of flushmount headlights. In the instructions on Toms web site he says how to wire it up so all four lights come on with the high beams. Well I wired it this way and only the high beams come one. Does anyone have the wiring diagram to get them set up right?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flush1.JPG"> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DrRodey||03-24-2001||09:42 PM||||I had the same problem when i got them.. all you have to do is put a paperclip between the connections in the module that connects to the highbeam switch so when you turn on the high beams it doesn't cut the power to the lows..  I know it's a vague answer but i was drunk when i did it and basically just experimented for a while and it ended up working.  Sorry if it doesn't help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||03-24-2001||10:12 PM||||Yea that is pretty vague. Im sorry I dont follow you on that one. Your talking about the module on the car right? Not the plug by the headlights?<P>Sorry if I sound stupid but Im not understanding. Maybe if I was drunk...hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Been there.....done that.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000003||DrRodey||03-24-2001||10:26 PM||||Ok i started thinking about it and i had to go check it out for myself.. so heres the scoop. When you take off the bottom panel of the dash under the steering column, on the side closest to the door there is a white module with a black plug,preaty much the only thing there.. comin out of the plug are six??? wires, yellow, pink and green.  (see pic one)  disconect that plug from the steering column.. it's kinda hard but it is possible  and use about 1" of a paperclip and connect the two connections as shown in pic two.  Bend the remainder of the paperclip flush and replace in it's original spot.. kinda a tight fit but it wokks.  <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/paperclip1.JPG"> <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/paperclip.JPG"> <P>I know the pictures are Extrememly bad but all i had for light was a handheld flashlight .If you have anymore questions please e-mail me<P>Dan.<P>[This message has been edited by DrRodey (edited 03-24-2001).]<P><BR>[This message has been edited by DrRodey (edited 03-24-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by DrRodey (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||03-24-2001||10:43 PM||||I was just out doing the same thing.<P>Laying on my back with a flashlight. I did use my haynes manual and found the switch you are talking about. Now I have to hunt around for a paper clip.<P><BR>Thanks for the pic. Really appreciate it.<P>Scott||||reg||1
